(formula "II ET" "M3" "=Lab!C51")
(cell "II ET" "N1" "ET, and: the lamp lit where a and b are both 1.")
(cell "II ET" "N2" "Given NON-ET, =1-x*y, and NON, proven at I, =1-x. Write y in J3.")
(cell "II ET" "N3" "De Morgan, 1847: not both is the one not or the other not, NON-ET(a,b) = VEL(NON a, NON b). Turn it around.")
(cell "II ET" "N7" "Space toggles the switch the selection stands on, 1 and 0 set it, a click toggles it; in the room 1 and 0 write themselves; T tests, R resets, N and P move.")
(cell "II ET" "N10" "A switch or a lamp written over is lost until Load, which loads every level afresh: R writes values, never a formula.")
(formula "II ET" "N8" "=\"Gates \"&Lab!E12&IF(Lab!Q12>0,\", \"&Lab!Q12&\" outside the set given, the first at \"&Lab!R12,\"\")&\"; the budget 3, the least known 2: \"&Lab!H12")
(formula "II ET" "N9" "=IF(Lab!N12=1,\"Calculemus: input \"&Lab!$B$6+1&\" of 4\",IF(Lab!B12=2,\"The test stops at input \"&Lab!C12+1&\" of 4, standing on the board: \"&IF(Lab!S12<>\"\",Lab!S12&\" holds an error: it reads a text, an emptied cell or an error.\",IF(Lab!L12=0,\"a switch written over does not follow the test. Load restores it, and empties every level.\",\"a lamp differs from its due.\")),IF(Lab!S12<>\"\",Lab!S12&\" holds an error: it reads a text, an emptied cell or an error.\"&\" Ex nihilo nihil fit.\",IF(Lab!B12=1,\"Quod erat demonstrandum: every one of its 4 inputs passes.\",\"T tests every input, an input a frame. Calculemus!\"))))")
