(cell "X MORA" "N1" "MORA, delay: A4 is a flip-flop. It holds q, and at a tick takes J3 as J3 stood. Write J3 so that q follows d a tick late.")
(cell "X MORA" "N2" "Given every gate proven, and ELIGE, proven at V, =IF(s,b,a). C ticks the clock: a tick is a frame, reading the frame before.")
(cell "X MORA" "N3" "T tests J3 at every d and every q: right for one tick from every state is right at every tick, by induction.")
(cell "X MORA" "N4" "Sine mora, the Romans said, without delay. Here the delay is the point: a tick is the language's twin, Lustre's pre.")
(cell "X MORA" "N7" "Space toggles the switch the selection stands on, 1 and 0 set it, a click toggles it; in the room 1 and 0 write themselves; T tests, R resets, N and P move.")
(cell "X MORA" "N10" "A switch or a lamp written over is lost until Load, which loads every level afresh: R writes values, never a formula.")
(formula "X MORA" "N8" "=\"Gates \"&Lab!E20&IF(Lab!Q20>0,\", \"&Lab!Q20&\" outside the set given, the first at \"&Lab!R20,\"\")&\"; the budget 2, the least known 1: \"&Lab!H20")
(formula "X MORA" "N9" "=IF(Lab!N20=1,\"Calculemus: input \"&Lab!$B$6+1&\" of 4\",IF(Lab!B20=2,\"The test stops at input \"&Lab!C20+1&\" of 4, standing on the board: \"&IF(Lab!S20<>\"\",Lab!S20&\" holds an error: it reads a text, an emptied cell or an error.\",IF(Lab!L20=0,\"a switch written over does not follow the test. Load restores it, and empties every level.\",\"a lamp differs from its due.\")),IF(Lab!S20<>\"\",Lab!S20&\" holds an error: it reads a text, an emptied cell or an error.\"&\" Ex nihilo nihil fit.\",IF(Lab!B20=1,\"Quod erat demonstrandum: every one of its 4 inputs passes.\",\"T tests every input, an input a frame. Calculemus!\"))))")
(formula "X MORA" "N11" "=IF(Lab!$E$2<>10,\"C ticks the clock once. G clears the flip-flops and runs the clock until they stand still.\",IF(Lab!$E$3=1,\"Currit, it runs: tick \"&Lab!$E$4,IF(Lab!$E$9=1,\"Stat, it stands: its last move at tick \"&Lab!$E$4-1&\".\",IF(Lab!$E$9=2,\"In aeternum: 2 ticks, no rest. 1 flip-flop holds 2 states, so one came twice: it never halts. A short tape answers Turing.\",\"C ticks the clock once. G clears the flip-flops and runs the clock until they stand still.\"))))")
