(formula "XII MEMORIA" "M3:M6" "=Lab!M51")
(cell "XII MEMORIA" "N1" "MEMORIA, memory: four flip-flops, a register: with load at 1, q' is d; with load at 0, q' is q. J3:J6, low bit first.")
(cell "XII MEMORIA" "N2" "Four of XI. Ctrl+K writes a formula over a range: (formula \"XII MEMORIA\" \"J3:J6\" \"=IF($A$3,A4,A8)\") fills all four.")
(cell "XII MEMORIA" "N3" "Cicero called memory the treasury of all things (De Oratore I.18). Here the treasury is four bits, with a lid.")
(cell "XII MEMORIA" "N7" "Space toggles the switch the selection stands on, 1 and 0 set it, a click toggles it; in the room 1 and 0 write themselves; T tests, R resets, N and P move.")
(cell "XII MEMORIA" "N10" "A switch or a lamp written over is lost until Load, which loads every level afresh: R writes values, never a formula.")
(formula "XII MEMORIA" "N8" "=\"Gates \"&Lab!E22&IF(Lab!Q22>0,\", \"&Lab!Q22&\" outside the set given, the first at \"&Lab!R22,\"\")&\"; the budget 6, the least known 4: \"&Lab!H22")
(formula "XII MEMORIA" "N9" "=IF(Lab!N22=1,\"Calculemus: input \"&Lab!$B$6+1&\" of 512\",IF(Lab!B22=2,\"The test stops at input \"&Lab!C22+1&\" of 512, standing on the board: \"&IF(Lab!S22<>\"\",Lab!S22&\" holds an error: it reads a text, an emptied cell or an error.\",IF(Lab!L22=0,\"a switch written over does not follow the test. Load restores it, and empties every level.\",\"a lamp differs from its due.\")),IF(Lab!S22<>\"\",Lab!S22&\" holds an error: it reads a text, an emptied cell or an error.\"&\" Ex nihilo nihil fit.\",IF(Lab!B22=1,\"Quod erat demonstrandum: every one of its 512 inputs passes.\",\"T tests every input, an input a frame. Calculemus!\"))))")
(formula "XII MEMORIA" "N11" "=IF(Lab!$E$2<>12,\"C ticks the clock once. G clears the flip-flops and runs the clock until they stand still.\",IF(Lab!$E$3=1,\"Currit, it runs: tick \"&Lab!$E$4,IF(Lab!$E$9=1,\"Stat, it stands: its last move at tick \"&Lab!$E$4-1&\".\",IF(Lab!$E$9=2,\"In aeternum: 16 ticks, no rest. 4 flip-flops hold 16 states, so one came twice: it never halts. A short tape answers Turing.\",\"C ticks the clock once. G clears the flip-flops and runs the clock until they stand still.\"))))")
