(formula "XIII NUMERA" "M3:M6" "=Lab!N51")
(cell "XIII NUMERA" "N1" "NUMERA, count: q' is q + inc, in four bits, and 0 at reset whatever else stands. J3:J6, low bit first; 15 + 1 is 0.")
(cell "XIII NUMERA" "N2" "Given every gate proven and ELIGE. A half adder a bit, the carry rippling, and a 0 chosen at reset: =IF(A3,0,x).")
(cell "XIII NUMERA" "N3" "With reset at 0 and inc at 1, press G: a counter has no rest, and N11 says what becomes of a machine that never stands still.")
(cell "XIII NUMERA" "N4" "Numera stellas, si potes: count the stars, if you can (Genesis 15:5, the Vulgate). This one counts to fifteen and begins again.")
(cell "XIII NUMERA" "N7" "Space toggles the switch the selection stands on, 1 and 0 set it, a click toggles it; in the room 1 and 0 write themselves; T tests, R resets, N and P move.")
(cell "XIII NUMERA" "N10" "A switch or a lamp written over is lost until Load, which loads every level afresh: R writes values, never a formula.")
