(cell "XIV RATIO" "N1" "RATIO, the reckoning: y in J3:J6 by op1 op0: 00 a ET b, 01 a VEL b, 10 a AUT b, 11 a + b, bit by bit, low bit first.")
(cell "XIV RATIO" "N2" "J7, the carry out of the sum, and 0 under every other op. Given every gate proven and ELIGE; no clock, and all 1,024 inputs.")
(cell "XIV RATIO" "N3" "Ratio is reckoning and reason in one Latin word, and Leibniz's calculus ratiocinator hoped to make them one thing.")
(cell "XIV RATIO" "N7" "Space toggles the switch the selection stands on, 1 and 0 set it, a click toggles it; in the room 1 and 0 write themselves; T tests, R resets, N and P move.")
(cell "XIV RATIO" "N10" "A switch or a lamp written over is lost until Load, which loads every level afresh: R writes values, never a formula.")
